      "label": "Artan Records",
      "cover": null,
      "links": [],
      "description": "A reconstruction of memory. Eight chapters return to what remained, rebuilt through the musician I have become.",
      "story": "Remnant returns to a formative period in Denmark: compositions, performances, people and unfinished thoughts. It preserves what survived without reproducing the past.\n\nThe project began with the private, unreleased Danish Expression of a Hijacked Plan, made in FL Studio. Remnant reconstructs that material in Logic Pro through memory, surviving music and a present perspective.\n\nRepetition becomes self-confrontation, questioning, distance, love and confession. Still closes the album with what remains.",
      "musicalDetails": "Intimate singer-songwriter, alternative, neoclassical, ambient and cinematic textures. Each track holds its own place within that space.",
      "productionProcess": "Restrained arrangements bring acoustic guitar, felt piano and close vocals into focus. Silence, decay and audible imperfections remain part of the music. Reconstruction and production take place in Logic Pro.",
      "relatedWork": "A standalone live acoustic recording of Still is already available. It is a separate master from the forthcoming Remnant studio recording.",
      "relatedReleaseIds": ["still-live-acoustic"],
      "tracks": [
        { "id": "station", "position": 1, "title": "Station", "status": "Upcoming", "originalTitle": "One Station Away", "key": "C-sharp minor", "tempo": "99 BPM reference", "feeling": "Endless Passage", "story": "Station opens the album through repetition and circular memory. A dark memory keeps returning without resolution. Its material preserves a connection to One Station Away.", "links": [] },
        { "id": "shadow", "position": 2, "title": "Shadow", "status": "Upcoming", "originalTitle": "Golden Teacher", "key": "A minor", "tempo": "92 BPM", "feeling": "Facing Within", "story": "Shadow turns inward, from repetition toward self-confrontation. The composition began as Golden Teacher and was later published as Shadow. The Remnant recording remains upcoming.", "links": [] },
        { "id": "wonder", "position": 3, "title": "Wonder", "status": "Upcoming", "originalTitle": "Wonderwhy", "key": "E-flat major (provisional)", "tempo": "72 BPM", "feeling": "Open Question", "story": "Wonder examines memory rather than simply returning to it. Reconstructed from Wonderwhy, it holds questioning, uncertainty and reflection.", "links": [] },
        { "id": "elsewhere", "position": 4, "title": "Elsewhere", "status": "Upcoming", "originalTitle": "Now You Are Talking Something Else", "key": "F minor (provisional)", "tempo": "66 BPM", "feeling": "Displaced Conversation", "story": "Two people may still be speaking while no longer occupying the same emotional place. Elsewhere reconstructs Now You Are Talking Something Else through distance and displacement.", "links": [] },
        { "id": "you", "position": 5, "title": "You", "status": "Upcoming", "originalTitle": "For You", "key": "A major", "tempo": "86 BPM reference", "feeling": "Pure Love", "story": "You returns to For You, originally performed with other musicians in Copenhagen. Guitar, piano and voice carry a direct expression of love and human closeness.", "links": [] },
        { "id": "lullaby", "position": 6, "title": "Lullaby", "status": "Upcoming", "originalTitle": "Simple Lullaby", "key": "A minor", "tempo": "130 BPM", "feeling": "Unspoken Love", "story": "Lullaby began before I met Filippa. After falling in love with her, it became an unspoken love song. I performed it while she was present, without telling her what it had come to mean. Within Remnant, it is for her: the last memory before distance.", "lyrics": "Sunlight dancing above,\npainting our sky so bright.\nSunshine hides in your eyes,\nraining down on my heart.\n\nWhen you're falling in love,\nfears start falling apart.\nStars sing a lullaby,\nangels begin to fly.\n\nLife is simple enough\nto make us fall in love.\nDiamonds shining above,\nsimple as we thought.\n\nIf you're falling in love,\ndark is replaced by light.\nMountains kneel on their knees,\nair feels good when you breathe.\n\nLife is simple enough\nto make us fall in love.\nDiamonds shining above,\nsimple as we thought.\n\nSimple as you smile,\nwhen you look in my eyes.\nI keep on holding on tight,\nwhen we are falling in love.", "links": [] },
        { "id": "filippa", "position": 7, "title": "Filippa", "status": "Upcoming", "key": "D minor", "tempo": "75 BPM", "feeling": "What I Never Told You", "story": "A new composition written in 2026. Filippa names the woman I loved but never directly told. Small moments survived: her smile, familiarity, anonymous notes and everything left unsaid. The resolution is not an imagined answer. It is finally speaking.", "musicalDetails": "Distance → The Armor → The Confession → The Notes → All These Years → The Climax → No More Hiding", "links": [] },
        { "id": "still", "position": 8, "title": "Still", "status": "Upcoming", "version": "Studio", "story": "Still looks back across years of distance and change. It asks what happened to the people involved and what survives after the original moment ends. Loved you becomes Love you.\n\nThis forthcoming studio master is separate from Still (Live Acoustic), with piano and a broader album arrangement intended.", "musicalDetails": "Remembering → Admission → Longing → Emotional Peak → What Remains. Voice gives way to an instrumental release before the final return.", "lyrics": "Circling back in time\nYou and I still wonder\nHow did all these years go by?\nDo we really know?\n\nIf I could bend the time\nI would go back to you\nBefore I lost myself\nBefore I lost you too\n\nLoved you\nLoved you\nLoved you\nLoved you\n\nWish you were here\nClose enough to stay\nIf you lost the way\nI'll find you someday\n\nWish you were here\nLike I never left\nTo love you every day\nBefore we fade away\n\nLoved you\nLoved you\nLoved you\nLoved you\n\nRunning through my mind\nAll the things I never said\nHow far did I go?\nStill I see you there\n\nEvery road I crossed\nLed me to the past\nEven from this far\nSome things echo back\n\nLoved you\nLoved you\nLoved you, still\n\nLove you", "links": [] }
      ]
    },
