      "id": "dream",
      "order": 4,
      "title": "Dream?",
      "language": "English",
      "copyright": "© 2026 Artan Davoodi",
      "story": "Dream? moves through learned emotional concealment, unsaid words, falling, mirrors and comparison. Its final recognition is that what appears outside may also reflect the self.",
      "lyrics": "You say man don't cry\nSo I learned how to hide\nDown in my dreams\nWhere I still try\n\nI kept words unsaid\nThey echoed anyway\nWatching the world fade\nDay after day\n\nI'm falling down\nWithout a parachute\nIgnited eyes\nWonder who is whom\n\nBreathing mirrors\nNo one set me free\nAwake in this dream\nWho's dream to be\n\nLike a dying tree\nRoots still try to hold\nEvery face that I look\nCompared against my own\n\nMy silence breaks apart\nI feel I need to know\nAll there is and all I see\nIs a reflection of my own",
